<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 1 September, from 1159 to 1969.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1159 CE <span class="tih-ago">867 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Adrian IV, the only English pope, dies at Anagni</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-adrian-iv">Nicholas Breakspear</a>, Pope Adrian IV, died after a stormy pontificate dominated by conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>. His death led to a disputed election and an 18-year schism.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1715 CE <span class="tih-ago">311 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XIV dies after 72 years on the throne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sun King died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> days before his 77th birthday, having reigned for 72 years, the longest of any major European monarch. His five-year-old great-grandson succeeded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv">Louis XV</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1807 CE <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Aaron Burr is acquitted of treason</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A jury in Richmond acquitted former Vice President Aaron Burr of plotting to wage war in the West. Chief Justice <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-marshall">John Marshall</a>'s strict reading of treason doomed Jefferson's prosecution.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1864 CE <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Confederates evacuate Atlanta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General John Bell Hood abandoned Atlanta, blowing up ammunition trains as he left, and Sherman's troops entered the next day. The capture of the rail hub revived Lincoln's re-election hopes.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1923 CE <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Kantō earthquake devastates Tokyo and Yokohama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake and the fires that followed destroyed much of Tokyo and Yokohama, killing more than 100,000 people. In the chaos, vigilantes murdered thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koreans">Koreans</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1939 CE <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces crossed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> at dawn without a declaration of war. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> declared war two days later, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1969 CE <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Muammar Gaddafi seizes power in Libya</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Junior army officers led by 27-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muammar-gaddafi">Muammar Gaddafi</a> overthrew King Idris in a bloodless coup. Gaddafi ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> for 42 years until his overthrow and death in 2011.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a></div></div></li></ol>
